COPY public.about_aboutsectioncontent (id, title, description, image, about_aminol_id) FROM stdin;
1	COMPANY PROFILE	ALCO LLC was entered into the state register on 5 May 2016. In the same year the company was granted resident status in the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park.\r\n\r\nConstruction of the ALCO LLC lubricant plant within the park began in 2016, and operations started on 15 December 2017 following the visit of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan to the park.\r\n\r\nThe plant is equipped with state-of-the-art German and Italian equipment, including fully automated production lines.\r\n\r\nOn the 3.5-hectare site allocated to ALCO LLC, a 5,000-tonne tank farm has been built for storing raw materials, intermediates and finished products, along with a 4,800 m² warehouse.\r\n\r\nTo improve packaging flexibility and strengthen internal supply, a plastic-container production unit was launched in 2019. Today ALCO LLC meets its needs entirely with high-quality plastic packaging of its own manufacture.\r\n\r\nSince 2019 the company’s scope has expanded to include technical fluids. A production area for coolant (antifreeze) with an annual capacity of 5,000 tonnes was installed, and a variety of antifreeze grades are now produced.\r\n\r\nIn 2020 the plant began manufacturing AdBlue®, a special non-toxic synthetic urea solution used to chemically reduce NOx emissions in diesel vehicles.\r\n\r\nThe plant houses an ISO/IEC 17025-accredited quality-assurance laboratory equipped with more than 30 modern instruments; tests are currently carried out for over 65 parameters.\r\n\r\nIn 2023 the necessary infrastructure was created to produce and store performance additives and, in line with modern requirements, to manufacture environmentally friendly plant-based bio-lubricants and fluids.\r\n\r\nFrom 2024 the plant’s annual production capacity has been raised to 100,000 tonnes.\r\n\r\nToday the company’s product portfolio comprises more than 1,000 unique items, with many new products in the commercialization pipeline.\r\n\r\nEngine oils produced by ALCO LLC are offered to customers with a warranty and can provide minimum oil-change intervals of 100,000 km in modern heavy-duty trucks and 30,000 km in passenger cars.\r\n\r\nIn addition, GE-approved locomotive oils that deliver maximum protection, fuel efficiency and engine durability—even under the harshest conditions—are supplied to the railway sector.\r\n\r\nHigh-performance oils play a crucial role in critical industries such as metalworking, power generation (including renewable wind energy and heat production), mining and cement, pulp and paper, textiles, and plastic and rubber processing. ALCO LLC offers a wide range of industrial lubricants tailored to each of these fields. Their high quality, consistent performance and long-term stability ensure efficient operation of industrial equipment, prevent technical failures and significantly extend service life.\r\n\r\nThus, thanks to its advanced technologies, extensive product range and international market strategy, ALCO LLC is today recognised as one of the largest specialised industrial enterprises for the production of lubricants and technical fluids in the South Caucasus and the wider region.	about_sections/17e8f2a7-1d8b-45ff-a347-807cea8d36b6-FR4A9020.jpg	1
2	BRAND HISTORY	“AMINOL” MEANS CONSISTENT POWER, RELIABLE PROTECTION, AND HIGH PERFORMANCE.\r\n\r\nCreated in 2017 under the “Made in Azerbaijan” label—fully in line with the economic policy pursued by President Ilham Aliyev—the AMINOL brand quickly earned solid reputation and trust in foreign markets.\r\n\r\nThe core advantage that sets the brand apart from competitors is its promise of consistent power, reliable protection, and high performance.\r\n\r\nAMINOL strikes an ideal balance between quality and price, making its products especially attractive to customers.	about_sections/a0be5c25-859a-4ffc-8b00-f46c98806ae9-8Z3A7187.jpg	1
3	KEY DEVELOPMENT MILESTONES	2017 - Registration of the “AMINOL” trademark in Azerbaijan\r\nThe trademark was entered into the state register by the Azerbaijan Copyright Agency, and production of the first product batches commenced the same year.\r\n\r\n2020 – 2022 - Obtaining OEM approvals and API / ACEA licenses\r\nTo boost competitiveness, more than 40 OEM approvals were secured, and the products were licensed under the classifications of the American Petroleum Institute (API) and the European Automobile Manufacturers’ Association (ACEA).\r\n\r\n2022 - Registration by WIPO\r\nFor international legal protection, “AMINOL” was registered in the WIPO Madrid System for the International Registration of Marks.\r\n2022 – 2023 - Portfolio enhancement & expansion\r\nIntensive R&D led to an expanded product portfolio: over 200 new, innovative products were developed and brought into production.\r\n\r\n2024 - Global recognition\r\nAMINOL attained international-brand status, exporting to more than 50 countries and becoming known worldwide for its “best value for money” concept.	about_sections/37f4882e-22ec-490d-a737-a68b396bdc76-8Z3A7411.jpg	1
4	MISSION & VISION	Mission\r\n\r\nTo combine our experience, knowledge and skills with modern technologies in order to deliver innovative, high-quality products and effective solutions (services) to our customers.\r\n\r\nVision\r\n\r\nTo achieve sustainable growth and become a globally recognised leader by pursuing responsible environmental practices, digital transformation, operational excellence and uncompromising business ethics.	about_sections/819be46c-6021-432a-9b0c-995b14e29fc6-FR4A9218.jpg	1
5	VALUES	•\tIntegrity & Ethics\r\nWe operate on the principles of transparency, accountability and honesty, building relationships of mutual trust with partners, customers and all stakeholders.\r\n\r\n\t•\tOperational Excellence\r\nWe continually optimise production processes, apply innovations and adhere to advanced industry standards to supply products of superior quality.\r\n\r\n\t•\tInnovation & Improvement\r\nWe invest in research and development (R&D), explore new technologies and constantly upgrade our products to meet evolving market demands.\r\n\r\n\t•\tCustomer Satisfaction\r\nWe study customer needs in depth and take the necessary measures to meet them, establishing long-term partnerships to provide top-level service and ensure customer satisfaction.\r\n\r\n\t•\tHealth, Safety & Well-being\r\nWe create a safe and healthy working environment that complies with international safety standards, treating employee welfare as a top priority.\r\n\r\n\t•\tSustainability & Social Responsibility\r\nGuided by ESG (environmental, social and governance) principles, we strive to protect the environment and contribute to society through ongoing tree-planting campaigns, the creation of green belts, donations to various public funds, and regular visits to orphanages and nursing homes.\r\n\r\n\t•\tCollaboration & Team Spirit\r\nWe believe in unity, mutual respect and open communication, fostering a workplace that strengthens team spirit. Every employee is encouraged to take initiative, create value and share in our collective success.\r\nSocial solidarity is one of our core values: we celebrate each team member’s milestones—birthdays included—and stand by one another in both joyful and challenging times.	about_sections/FR4A9674.jpg	1
\.
COPY public.about_documentscertification (id, title, description) FROM stdin;
1	Implementation of ISO standards	The company’s integrated management systems have been audited by a UKAS-accredited certification body and certified to the following international standards:\r\n\t•\tISO 9001:2015 – Quality Management System\r\n\t•\tISO 14001:2015 – Environmental Management System\r\n\t•\tISO 45001:2018 – Occupational Health & Safety Management System\r\n\r\nPreparatory work is under way to introduce ISO 27001 “Information security, cybersecurity and privacy protection – Information security management systems”.
2	REACH registration	The base oils that form the main component of finished products are registered under the EU’s REACH regulation, allowing unrestricted export of the products to EU member states.
3	API & ACEA licences	Licences have been obtained from the American Petroleum Institute (API) and the European Automobile Manufacturers’ Association (ACEA) to confirm that the products meet the classifications defined by these bodies.
4	Membership of ATIEL & UKLA	ALCO LLC is a member of ATIEL (Technical Association of the European Lubricants Industry) and UKLA (United Kingdom Lubricants Association). These memberships demonstrate that the company’s products are manufactured in full compliance with international classifications and high industry standards.
5	OEM APPROVALS	The products have been evaluated for conformity with the specifications of more than 40 original equipment manufacturers (OEMs), including Deutz AG, Volvo Group, General Motors, Mercedes-Benz AG, General Electric, Volkswagen AG, Caterpillar, Cummins, Ford Motor Company, Stellantis N.V. (Chrysler) and MAN Truck & Bus SE, and the corresponding approvals have been obtained.\r\n\r\nWork is also in progress to secure approvals from additional OEMs such as BMW AG, Dr. Ing. h.c. F. Porsche AG, Tata Motors (Jaguar / Land Rover), Opel Automobile GmbH, Bosch Rexroth, Parker Denison, Eaton, Fives Cincinnati, Afnor, Krauss Maffei, Husky, Palfinger and others.
\.
