1	Alco LLC, a resident of the Sumgait Chemical Industrial Park, has begun exporting lubricants and coolants to European countries, including Germany, Italy, the United Kingdom, Romania, and Bulgaria.\r\n\r\nAccording to information from the Industrial Park provided to APA-Economics, more than 2,000 tons of products have been shipped to these countries in the initial phase, with plans to increase this volume to 10,000 tons in the next stage.\r\n\r\nIt should be noted that the enterprise, with an investment value of $15 million, employs up to 100 people. From the start of its operations until the end of 2021, the company produced over 36,000 tons of products, of which 6,000 tons were sold on the domestic market and 30,000 tons were exported.\r\n\r\nThe manufactured products are mainly exported to countries such as Turkey, Georgia, Ukraine, Iraq, Lebanon, Poland, Moldova, Turkmenistan, and others.	news/marjaaz1539786768aminol2_Y0WO66G.jpg	10
2	A large part of our lands occupied by Armenia was liberated from enemy control through the bravery of the Azerbaijani Army on the battlefield, under the leadership of the victorious Commander-in-Chief, President Ilham Aliyev, and as a result of successful diplomatic efforts.\r\n\r\nDuring the battles, the Azerbaijani Army suffered over 3,000 martyrs, and more than 10,000 of our wounded veterans are in need of treatment. We honor the memory of our fallen heroes and wish a speedy recovery and good health to our veterans.\r\n\r\nBy the Decree of the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan, the Karabakh Revival Fund was established to support sustainable resettlement, provide decent and modern living conditions, carry out reconstruction, restoration, and development works in all areas, and ensure safe living, efficient operations, and the continuous improvement of welfare in the liberated territories.\r\n\r\nFulfilling its patriotic duty, the AMINOL family has once again donated AZN 20,000 to the Karabakh Revival Fund.\r\n\r\nPreviously, AMINOL has supported the Armed Forces Assistance Fund, the YAŞAT Foundation, and the COVID-19 Response Fund, thereby continuing to contribute to the state and its citizens through acts of patriotism.\r\n\r\n“AMINOL” branded lubricants are produced using the most advanced German technology at the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park, on a site allocated to “ALCO” LLC.	news/image_7_w6qHSCq.png	9
3	The Republic of Azerbaijan is currently experiencing some of the most historic and proud days of its independence. A significant portion of our territories, occupied by Armenia for 28 years, has been liberated from enemy occupation through the leadership of the victorious Supreme Commander-in-Chief, Mr. Ilham Aliyev, the valor of the Azerbaijani Army on the battlefield, and diplomatic negotiations. The Azerbaijani Army endured over 3,000 martyrs in these battles, and thousands of our veterans require medical treatment. We extend our deepest condolences to our martyrs and wish our veterans swift recovery and good health.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the global Coronavirus (Covid-19) pandemic, which has raged for nearly a year, has also negatively impacted the Azerbaijani economy. Despite these challenges, the strong unity of the people around the President of the Republic of Azerbaijan has further strengthened our state. The fact that every citizen has fulfilled their duty in this challenging situation is a profoundly positive and vital development.\r\n\r\nDuring this period of pandemic and war, the team at ALCO LLC's AMINOL lubricant plant did not hesitate to offer its support. AMINOL consistently provided aid to the "Fund to Support Fight Against Coronavirus (Covid-19)" and the "Armed Forces Aid Fund."\r\n\r\nBeyond financial and moral support on the home front during Azerbaijan's glorious victory in the war, three AMINOL employees volunteered for military service, responding to the call of the Supreme Commander-in-Chief, and fought on the front lines.\r\n\r\nAMINOL continues to fulfill its duty of state support and patriotism by making donations to the "YAŞAT" Fund, established to support the families of martyrs.	news/image_6_FomoTtW.png	8
4	ALCO LLC, a manufacturer of lubricants, has transferred 100,000 Azerbaijani Manats (AZN) to the Armed Forces Aid Fund. This information was confirmed to Marja by the company.\r\n\r\n"Karabakh is Azerbaijan!"	news/image_5_ZKf7EIg.png	7
5	Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park, Azerbaijan – AMINOL is significantly expanding the production of its "Made in Azerbaijan" lubricant products, leveraging cutting-edge German technology within the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park.\r\n\r\nIn just two years since its operational launch, AMINOL has established direct partnerships with leading global raw material suppliers, including Lubrizol, Afton Chemical, BASF, Infineum, Chevron, BRB, ENI, and Evonik. Throughout this period, the company's highly skilled local and international teams have remained focused on delivering high-quality products and enhancing export capabilities.\r\n\r\nThis strategic focus led to the acquisition of ISO 9001-2015, ISO 14001-2015, and ISO 17025 certifications through the internationally recognized UKAS system. Furthermore, in collaboration with General Electric (GE), AMINOL stands as one of only two companies in the CIS region certified for 4 LL (Long Life) diesel engines.\r\n\r\nMost recently, AMINOL successfully obtained the prestigious API (American Petroleum Institute) certification, a paramount international quality benchmark for motor oil manufacturers. Despite its relatively short operational history, AMINOL lubricants are already exported to 14 countries. The company anticipates expanding its global reach to even more markets starting from the new year.\r\n\r\nAMINOL lubricants produced with the API certification will deliver significant benefits, including enhanced fuel efficiency, extended service life for engines and equipment, and reduced environmental pollution.\r\n\r\nThe AMINOL team expresses its sincere gratitude to its valued partners, particularly Lubrizol, BASF, Infineum, and British Petroleum Azerbaijan (BP), for their rigorous standards and collaborative efforts that have been instrumental in these achievements.\r\n\r\nThe AMINOL team extends its best wishes to all for the upcoming World Azerbaijanis Solidarity Day and New Year, desiring good health and continued success.	news/image_4_g20JXhD.png	6
6	Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park, Azerbaijan – AMINOL is significantly expanding the production of its "Made in Azerbaijan" lubricant products, leveraging cutting-edge German technology within the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park.\r\n\r\nIn just two years since its operational launch, AMINOL has established direct partnerships with leading global raw material suppliers, including Lubrizol, Afton Chemical, BASF, Infineum, Chevron, BRB, ENI, and Evonik. Throughout this period, the company's highly skilled local and international teams have remained focused on delivering high-quality products and enhancing export capabilities.\r\n\r\nThis strategic focus led to the acquisition of ISO 9001-2015, ISO 14001-2015, and ISO 17025 certifications through the internationally recognized UKAS system. Furthermore, in collaboration with General Electric (GE), AMINOL stands as one of only two companies in the CIS region certified for 4 LL (Long Life) diesel engines.\r\n\r\nMost recently, AMINOL successfully obtained the prestigious API (American Petroleum Institute) certification, a paramount international quality benchmark for motor oil manufacturers. Despite its relatively short operational history, AMINOL lubricants are already exported to 14 countries. The company anticipates expanding its global reach to even more markets starting from the new year.\r\n\r\nAMINOL lubricants produced with the API certification will deliver significant benefits, including enhanced fuel efficiency, extended service life for engines and equipment, and reduced environmental pollution.\r\n\r\nThe AMINOL team expresses its sincere gratitude to its valued partners, particularly Lubrizol, BASF, Infineum, and British Petroleum Azerbaijan (BP), for their rigorous standards and collaborative efforts that have been instrumental in these achievements.\r\n\r\nThe AMINOL team extends its best wishes to all for the upcoming World Azerbaijanis Solidarity Day and New Year, desiring good health and continued success.	news/image_3_MiQjdyk.png	5
7	The production of “AMINOL” branded lubricants began on December 15, 2017, at the area allocated to “ALCO” LLC in the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park, using the most advanced German technology. This milestone coincided with the visit of President Ilham Aliyev to Sumgayit city.\r\n\r\nThe plant has an annual production capacity of 30,000 tons and an investment volume of 10 million USD. The facility mainly produces engine oils, industrial oils, hydraulic oils, compressor oils, turbine oils, transmission oils, and marine oils.\r\n\r\nFor over a year, the AMINOL Lubricant Plant has been the first local manufacturer producing high-quality aviation oil that meets international standards.\r\n\r\nRecently, the AMINOL Lubricant Plant received the “Fundamental Approval” — a primary certification — from the global giant General Electric (GE) for its AMINOL M-14D2 locomotive oil.\r\n\r\nWith this achievement, AMINOL became the second company in the CIS region, after Lukoil, authorized to produce the specially formulated 4LL (Long Life) AMINOL M-14D2 locomotive oil.	news/image_2_FI8FQgo.png	4
8	(®) AMINOL Lubricant Plant Representatives Attend International Lubrication Conference and Receive Certification\r\nEmel Kuşku, Production Manager of the AMINOL Lubricant Plant, and Aytan Maharramli, Chief Laboratory Technician, participated in the “Lubrication Fundamentals Conference” organized by Lubrizol Corporation at its Hazelwood Research & Development Center in the United Kingdom from April 9–11.\r\n\r\nFounded in 1947, the Lubrizol Hazelwood center is one of the world’s leading facilities for research and testing of chemical additives. It conducts global field tests on passenger and commercial vehicles, marine vessels, and hydraulic systems—ensuring performance, durability, fuel efficiency, and OEM compliance.\r\n\r\nDuring the three-day conference, in-depth sessions and discussions were held on topics such as:\r\n\r\nBase oils and additives\r\n\r\nTransmission systems and automotive engines\r\n\r\nTractor and industrial gear oils\r\n\r\nHydraulic and compressor lubricants\r\n\r\nAntifreeze technologies and fuels\r\n\r\nOn the final day, participants toured the Hazelwood R&D Center, where they observed chemical and physical testing of additives, testing equipment, and mechanical trials conducted on engines.\r\n\r\nThe event was attended by representatives of global industry leaders, including Valvoline, ESCOM, Morris Lubricants, Gazprom, and LUKOIL.\r\n\r\nAt the conclusion of the event, both Emel Kuşku and Aytan Maharramli were awarded international certificates in recognition of their successful participation.	news/image_1_fOmuDQC.png	3
9	(®) "Aminol" Lubricant Plant Receives ISO 9001:2015 Certification\r\n"Alco" LLC, the manufacturer of "Aminol" lubricants, became the first company in Azerbaijan to transition from ISO 9001:2008 to the new ISO 9001:2015 quality management standard on September 24, 2018.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, Aminol is the first local Azerbaijani brand to receive ISO 9001:2015 certification from UKAS Management Systems, one of the world’s most recognized international certification bodies.\r\n\r\nKnown for its high quality and competitive pricing, Aminol is also set to launch production of the MS-20 aviation oil this month.\r\n\r\nCurrently, Alco continues to produce a range of lubricants with the support and approval of Italy’s ENI Group, including:\r\n\r\nAminol Advance AC4\r\n\r\nAminol Industrial Hydraulic HLP\r\n\r\nAminol Transmission TN1 / TN2 / TN3 / TN4 / TN5\r\n\r\nAminol Premium PMD API CH-4 / CI-4\r\n\r\nAnd other specialized products.	news/marjaaz1539786768aminol2_Vdzcn8X.jpg	2
10	Another Lubricant Manufacturer Launched in Azerbaijan\r\n\r\nAccording to Marja, a new lubricant manufacturer has started operations in Azerbaijan. The company in question is “Alco Lubricant Company” LLC, a resident of the Sumgayit Chemical Industrial Park.\r\n\r\nEstablished with an investment of $10 million, the Lubricant Plant aims to produce 30,000 tons of various high-quality lubricants annually. These products are intended for use in the automotive, aviation, marine, agriculture, industrial, and energy sectors.\r\n\r\nBuilt using German technology, the facility will provide permanent employment for 100 people.\r\n\r\nThe lubricants will be marketed under the brand name AMINOL.\r\n\r\nThe plant offers a wide range of more than 70 product types tailored for different industries, including:\r\n\r\nEngine oils\r\n\r\nHydraulic oils\r\n\r\nTransmission oils\r\n\r\nIndustrial oils\r\n\r\nMarine oils\r\n\r\nOils for heavy construction and agricultural machinery\r\n\r\nLubricants for various other equipment and applications\r\n\r\nALCO Lubricants also plans to export its products to Turkey, Germany, Georgia, and other CIS countries.\r\n\r\nIt’s worth noting that Technol is another well-known local lubricant brand in Azerbaijan.	news/image_9Bv2HTU.png	1
